A footnote definition interrupts a footnote's paragraph.
````
[^n]: note
[^m]: other

x[^n] y[^m]
.
<p>x<a id="fnref1" href="#fn1" role="doc-noteref"><sup>1</sup></a> y<a id="fnref2" href="#fn2" role="doc-noteref"><sup>2</sup></a></p>
<section role="doc-endnotes">
<hr>
<ol>
<li id="fn1">
<p>note<a href="#fnref1" role="doc-backlink">↩︎</a></p>
</li>
<li id="fn2">
<p>other<a href="#fnref2" role="doc-backlink">↩︎</a></p>
</li>
</ol>
</section>
````

A reference definition interrupts a footnote's paragraph.
````
[^n]: note
[r]: /url

x[^n] [r][r]
.
<p>x<a id="fnref1" href="#fn1" role="doc-noteref"><sup>1</sup></a> <a href="/url">r</a></p>
<section role="doc-endnotes">
<hr>
<ol>
<li id="fn1">
<p>note<a href="#fnref1" role="doc-backlink">↩︎</a></p>
</li>
</ol>
</section>
````

